block.text:
No backend here. We can use actor_type as input with datalist options ['user','admin','system','agent','tool']? Hmm maybe backend uses `user`, `system`, `scheduler`? Unknown. Let's use a text input with a datalist containing common values and free input. Requirement only mandates additional fields; type not mandated. Good.

Now, `canViewAll` prop can change dynamically. Use watch on props.canViewAll:
```
watch(() => props.canViewAll, (allowed) => {
  if (!allowed && scope.value === 'all') {
    scope.value = 'own'
    void load()
  } else if (allowed && !loaded.value && !loading.value) void load()
})
```
When mounted, load own. If canViewAll starts false and later true, no reload needed (own data valid). If scope all and canViewAll turns false, switch to own and reload (filters global fields ignored in build).

Maybe expose mode buttons:
```
<div class="scope-switch" role="group" aria-label="审计范围">
  <button :class="{active: scope==='own'}">我的审计</button>
  <button v-if="canViewAll" ...>全局审计</button>
</div>
```
Could be a segmented control.

When switching scope: reset items and load; also clear global-only filter fields? Perhaps keep, but own ignores them. If switch back, values retained. Fine. Maybe clearing is more predictable. Not necessary.

Filters panel: should be collapsible? Keep simple grid. This is a settings panel; include title "审计日志" and endpoint hint `/api/v1/audit-logs · /api/v1/admin/audit-logs`. Info bar with text about coverage. Use `.desc`.

For `applied` filters vs form state: If we pass reactive filters directly on apply, fine. When query button clicked, set current filters snapshot. Otherwise if user edits input after loading, not auto reload. We can just build from current state at click. Load more must use the same filters as initial load, otherwise edited-but-not-applied fields could change paging. Snapshot is better:
```
